{"name":"Blue Square","hex":"#508a9a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue square","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["On a trail map, an indicator of a ski slope of intermediate difficulty, steeper and narrower than a green circle, and with a gradient of 25–40%."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_square"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Rank Group","blocks":[{"text":"The Rank Group plc is a gambling company based in the United Kingdom. Rank was involved in the cinema and motion picture industry until 2006, and continues to use the Gongman logo originally used by the Rank Organisation's film distribution subsidiary General Film Distributors. Its brands now include Mecca Bingo, and Grosvenor Casinos, the UK's largest casino operator."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/Rank_group_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rank_Group"},{"title":"Piste","blocks":[{"text":"A piste is a marked trail or path down a mountain for snow skiing, snowboarding, or other mountain sports."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Mindersjochabfahrt.JPG/330px-Mindersjochabfahrt.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piste"},{"title":"Square","blocks":[{"text":"In geometry, a square is a regular quadrilateral. It has four straight sides of equal length and four equal angles. Squares are special cases of rectangles, which have four equal angles, and of rhombuses, which have four equal sides. As with all rectangles, a square's angles are right angles, making adjacent sides perpendicular. The area of a square is the side length multiplied by itself, and so in algebra, multiplying a number by itself is called squaring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg/330px-Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Mecca_Bingo_and_Grosvenor_Casino%2C_St_Thomas%27s_Road%2C_Huddersfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1774776.jpg/500px-Mecca_Bingo_and_Grosvenor_Casino%2C_St_Thomas%27s_Road%2C_Huddersfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1774776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Mecca_Bingo_and_Grosvenor_Casino%2C_St_Thomas%27s_Road%2C_Huddersfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1774776.jpg/500px-Mecca_Bingo_and_Grosvenor_Casino%2C_St_Thomas%27s_Road%2C_Huddersfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1774776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grosvenor Casino and Mecca Bingo in Huddersfield","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMecca_Bingo_and_Grosvenor_Casino%2C_St_Thomas's_Road%2C_Huddersfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1774776.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi